# Cloudflare Pages custom headers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Cloudflare Pages keeps serving the temporary address
# (pyt-website.pages.dev) even after a real custom domain is added. Both
# addresses serve the SAME build. Left alone, search engines index both and
# treat the real site as a duplicate of the temporary one.
#
# The rules below tell search engines not to index anything served on a
# *.pages.dev address. They are matched on the HOSTNAME, so they apply ONLY
# to the temporary address and NEVER to the real domain.
#
# THIS IS DELIBERATELY HOST-SCOPED. Do not replace it with a robots.txt
# containing "Disallow: /" — that file cannot tell the two addresses apart
# and would block the real domain too, silently, with no error anywhere.
#
# Also note: do NOT add a robots.txt that blocks crawling of these pages.
# "noindex" only works if the crawler is allowed to fetch the page and read
# this header. Blocking the crawl stops it ever seeing the noindex.
#
# NOTHING NEEDS TO CHANGE IN THIS FILE AT LAUNCH. It is self-correcting.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The main temporary address.
https://pyt-website.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# Per-deployment preview addresses, e.g. a1b2c3d4.pyt-website.pages.dev
https://:preview.pyt-website.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# Any other *.pages.dev address this project is ever served on.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
